Upstream bug: the "invalid alias" warning concatenates `path` directly, but
`path` is an `obsidian.Path` TABLE here -- so the warning itself raises
"attempt to concatenate local 'path' (a table value)". That error propagates
out of `Note.from_file_async` and aborts the WHOLE search, so one bad note
kills every result instead of producing one warning about that note.

The sibling `tags` branch twelve lines below already uses `tostring(path)`;
this branch was simply missed.

How you get a non-string alias in the first place: an unquoted alias
containing ": " is valid YAML for a MAP, so

    aliases:
      - Eval SOTA: Significance

parses as `{ ["Eval SOTA"] = "Significance" }` -- a table, not a string --
which lands in exactly this branch.

--- a/lua/obsidian/note.lua
+++ b/lua/obsidian/note.lua
@@ -523,7 +523,7 @@ Note.from_lines = function(lines, path, opts)
               else
                 log.warn(
                   "Invalid alias value found in frontmatter for "
-                    .. path
+                    .. tostring(path)
                     .. ". Expected string, found "
                     .. type(alias)
                     .. "."
